.TH "SQL2CSV" "1" "Aug 16, 2024" "2.2.0" "csvkit"
.SH NAME
sql2csv \- sql2csv Documentation
.SH DESCRIPTION
.sp
Executes arbitrary commands against a SQL database and outputs the results as a CSV:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
usage: sql2csv [\-h] [\-v] [\-l] [\-V] [\-\-db CONNECTION_STRING]
               [\-\-engine\-option ENGINE_OPTION ENGINE_OPTION]
               [\-\-execution\-option EXECUTION_OPTION EXECUTION_OPTION]
               [\-\-query QUERY] [\-e ENCODING] [\-H]
               [\-\-null\-value [NULL_VALUE]]
               [FILE]

Execute a SQL query on a database and output the result to a CSV file.

positional arguments:
  FILE                  The file to use as the SQL query. If FILE and \-\-query
                        are omitted, the query is piped data via STDIN.

optional arguments:
  \-h, \-\-help            show this help message and exit
  \-\-db CONNECTION_STRING
                        A SQLAlchemy connection string to connect to a
                        database.
  \-\-engine\-option ENGINE_OPTION ENGINE_OPTION
                        A keyword argument to SQLAlchemy\(aqs create_engine(), as
                        a space\-separated pair. This option can be specified
                        multiple times. For example: thick_mode True
  \-\-execution\-option EXECUTION_OPTION EXECUTION_OPTION
                        A keyword argument to SQLAlchemy\(aqs
                        execution_options(), as a space\-separated pair. This
                        option can be specified multiple times. For example:
                        stream_results True
  \-\-query QUERY         The SQL query to execute. Overrides FILE and STDIN.
  \-e ENCODING, \-\-encoding ENCODING
                        Specify the encoding of the input query file.
  \-H, \-\-no\-header\-row   Do not output column names.
  \-\-null\-value [NULL_VALUE]
                        Write SQL NULL values as this marker, so that NULL is
                        distinguishable from empty strings and from strings
                        that literally contain the marker. If the option is
                        given without a value, the default marker "\eN" is
                        used. Non\-NULL values beginning with the marker are
                        escaped by doubling the marker prefix, making the
                        export reversible: a field equal to the marker reads
                        back as NULL, a field beginning with two markers reads
                        back as the text after the first marker, and every
                        other field reads back as\-is. The marker must be
                        non\-empty and must not contain line breaks. By
                        default (without this option), NULL is written as an
                        empty field.
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH EXAMPLES
.sp
Load sample data into a table using \fI\%csvsql\fP and then query it using \fIsql2csv\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
csvsql \-\-db \(dqsqlite:///dummy.db\(dq \-\-tables \(dqtest\(dq \-\-insert examples/dummy.csv
sql2csv \-\-db \(dqsqlite:///dummy.db\(dq \-\-query \(dqselect * from test\(dq
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Load data about financial aid recipients into PostgreSQL. Then find the three states that received the most, while also filtering out empty rows:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
createdb recipients
csvsql \-\-db \(dqpostgresql:///recipients\(dq \-\-tables \(dqfy09\(dq \-\-insert examples/realdata/FY09_EDU_Recipients_by_State.csv
sql2csv \-\-db \(dqpostgresql:///recipients\(dq \-\-query \(dqselect * from fy09 where \e\(dqState Name\e\(dq != \(aq\(aq order by fy09.\e\(dqTOTAL\e\(dq limit 3\(dq
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
You can even use it as a simple SQL calculator (in this example an in\-memory SQLite database is used as the default):
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
sql2csv \-\-query \(dqselect 300 * 47 % 14 * 27 + 7000\(dq
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The connection string \fI\%accepts parameters\fP\&. For example, to set the encoding of a MySQL database:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
sql2csv \-\-db \(aqmysql://user:pass@host/database?charset=utf8\(aq \-\-query \(dqSELECT myfield FROM mytable\(dq
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Distinguish NULL from empty strings
.sp
By default, a SQL NULL is written as an empty CSV field, which is indistinguishable from an empty string. Use the \fB\-\-null\-value\fP option to write NULL as an explicit marker instead:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
sql2csv \-\-db \(dqsqlite:///dummy.db\(dq \-\-null\-value \-\-query \(dqselect * from test\(dq
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Without a value, the marker is \fB\eN\fP, the same convention used by MySQL\(aqs \fBSELECT ... INTO OUTFILE\fP and PostgreSQL\(aqs \fBCOPY ... WITH NULL\fP. A different marker can be given:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
sql2csv \-\-db \(dqsqlite:///dummy.db\(dq \-\-null\-value \(aq@NULL@\(aq \-\-query \(dqselect * from test\(dq
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The export is reversible. The encoding rule, applied uniformly to every row of every batch (including streaming, multi\-batch result sets), is:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
A SQL NULL is written as the marker.
.IP \(bu 2
A non\-NULL value that begins with the marker is written with the marker doubled at the front, so that the marker can appear inside real values without ambiguity. For example, with the default marker, the text \fB\eN\fP is written \fB\eN\eN\fP, and \fB\eN suffix\fP is written \fB\eN\eN suffix\fP.
.IP \(bu 2
Every other value (including the empty string) is written unchanged.
.UNINDENT
.sp
To read the data back, treat a field equal to the marker as NULL, remove one leading marker from a field that begins with two markers, and leave every other field as\-is. The empty string therefore stays an empty string, and the literal text \fBNULL\fP stays the text \fBNULL\fP.
.sp
When loading the CSV with \fI\%csvsql\fP or \fI\%in2csv\fP, the same marker can be passed to \fB\-\-null\-value\fP (with \fB\-\-blanks\fP to keep empty strings empty):
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
csvsql \-\-db \(dqsqlite:///dummy.db\(dq \-\-tables \(dqtest\(dq \-\-insert \-\-null\-value \(aq\eN\(aq \-\-blanks export.csv
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
